    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2b1bc549_0abc8db0",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 736,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000187
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-10T01:24:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Add:\n\nif (flags \u0026 SYSTEM_RESET_WAIT_EXT) {\n  /* Wait 10 seconds for external reset */\n  for (i \u003d 0; i \u003c 1000; i++) {\n    watchdog_reload();\n    udelay(10000);\n}\n\nThen drop through to spinning (which will watchdog after a couple seconds).  That way, we won\u0027t hang forever if external reset doesn\u0027t come in.\n\nNote that we must use udelay() not usleep() because interrupts have been disabled.",
      "parentUuid": "58814702_40b3e642",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 734,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 736,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "691964095feea2c08ab15becfc476107b586b091",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f637365a_35b6d169",
        "filename": "chip/npcx/system.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 736,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-11-10T21:01:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we should just wait and kick the watchdog forever. If we have the print, I think it should be clear that the device is waiting for external reset.\n\nIf a user/developer notices their EC is stuck, they\u0027ll probably assert EC_RST_L anyways.",
      "parentUuid": "2b1bc549_0abc8db0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 734,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 736,
        "endChar": 3
      },
      "revId": "691964095feea2c08ab15becfc476107b586b091",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
